At 04:53 PM 7/6/03 +0300, Robin Turner wrote:
>MorphemeAddict@wmconnect.com wrote:
> > how does one convey the idea of "intelligent" or "smart" in lojban?  i
> > don't see any gismu or lujvo that convey that idea.
>
>A surprising omission - it's not in the gismu list, Nora's lujvo list or
>jbovlaste.  The best I can come up with is "xaupei" (xamgu pensi) but
>xamgu is far too vague.  I looked for "efficient" and "effective" but
>couldn't find anything for those either

"Smart" is polysemous.

Nora and I have used mencre (menli certu)

I would consider for
efficient: sutcre (sutra certu)
effective: ja'ecre (jalge certu)

so you can put menli or men- in front of either of those
or pensi or pes-/pei-

